                <section id="Onboarding">
                    <h1 class="title">Onboarding</h1>
                    <div class="accordion_data">
                        <div class="accordion">
                            <div class="accordion-item">
                                <div class="accordion-header">
                                    <div class="accordion-title">What is On Boarding Process in Minop?</div>
                                    <div class="accordion-icon">
                                        <i class="fa fa-angle-down" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                                <div class="accordion-body">
                                    <ul>
                                        <li>First, open this website <a href="https://app.minopcloud.com/">minopcloud.com</a></li>
                                        <li>Click on Login -> Time</li>
                                        <li>Click on the Admin Section, then click on the 'Sign Up' Button.</li>
                                        <li>Fill in your company's details properly.</li>
                                        <li>After filling in all the details, click on the register button. If all is correct, you will receive an alert indicating 'Registration Successful'.</li>
                                        <li>You will receive an email on your defined email ID with a button to activate your account.</li>
                                        <li>When you click on that, your account will be created in the database, and you can start exploring Minop features and functionality.</li>
                                        <li>Afterward, login with that email ID, and the first page you will see is the system setting page.</li>
                                        <li>In the first step, set your company info like email ID, contact info, GST number (if possible), etc.</li>
                                        <li>
                                            After filling that out, when you click on the next button, the company setting page will open. Here, you need to set some functionalities that apply globally across all employees or other admins, such as:
                                            <ul>
                                                <li>Date Format: There is a dropdown related to the date format where you select the format according to your preference, e.g., dd-mm-yyyy. Once selected, your entire data will show in this format.</li>
                                            </ul>
                                            Fill in and set the related features, and when you click on the finish button, you will be redirected to the 'Admin Dashboard' page.
                                        </li>
                                        <li>The next step is to set proper shifts according to your company time and customize them for different employees.</li>
                                        <li>For that, go to Shift -> Shift from the menu.</li>
                                        <li>
                                            Click on the '+'. After clicking the '+' sign, a modal will open. In that, fill in all the fields related to your company, such as:
                                            <ul>
                                                <li>Shift Name -> (Day Shift)</li>
                                                <li>Start Time: End Time -> 00:09 / 18:00</li>
                                                <li>There are other extra fields where you can set things like minimum hours for half-day, etc.</li>
                                            </ul>
                                            Now this shift is created, and when you apply it to any employee, all their data will be shown according to this timing.
                                        </li>
                                        <li>The next step is to set policies according to your company that are applicable to the employees you assign them to.</li>
                                        <li>Go to Policy -> HR Policy.</li>
                                        <li>Click on '+'. A modal will open!</li>
                                        <li>
                                           <p> Now, fill the fields according to your policy. For example:</p>
                                            <ul>
                                                <li>Policy Name -> General Policy</li>
                                                <li>Below that, you have many options like giving a full week off or other similar options.</li>
                                                <li>There are also half-day rules where you can customize a half-day on a particular day of the week.</li>
                                                <li>There is an option for giving overtime to employees or not.</li>
                                                <li>After filling in the necessary fields, click on the 'Next' button.</li>
                                                <li>On the next screen, there are many parameters like 'Out punch should be accepted at the last hour,' e.g., 12 (after that, the punch will not be accepted).</li>
                                                <li>If you want to give grace time between in-time and out-time, that is also possible.</li>
                                                <li>
                                                    Select the application mode. There are three modes, but mainly we work with:
                                                    <ul>
                                                        <li><b>Fix:</b> In this, whatever punch mode we get from the device or hardware side, we set it as it is in our software. For example, if the first punch is 'IN' and the second punch is also 'IN,' we set it as it is.</li>
                                                        <li><b>Auto:</b> In this, we automatically change the punch mode. For example, if we get the first punch as 'IN' and the second punch as 'IN' from hardware, we interchange it to 'OUT' from our side.</li>
                                                    </ul>
                                                </li>
                                                <li>
                                                    After that, on the next step, you will have two major modules that you need to set according to your policies:
                                                    <ul>
                                                        <li><b>Overtime Calculation:</b> Set the minimum overtime, how it's calculated with shifts, and understand it easily.</li>
                                                        <li><b>Sandwich Allowance:</b> If you want to impose a sandwich policy in the selected policy, you can set it. There are also customized rules that you can sanction below the given list.</li>
                                                    </ul>
                                                </li>
                                                <li>
                                                    In the next step, define any attendance rules you want to apply, such as:
                                                    <ul>
                                                        <li>If any employee is late checking in, automatically set that day as a half-day.</li>
                                                        <li>Similarly, set rules for present, absent, and half-day conditions.</li>
                                                        <li>If you want to give 'X' hours of grace time, that is also possible.</li>
                                                    </ul>
                                                </li>
                                                <li>This is the whole module where you can set policies for the company.</li>
                                            </ul>
                                        </li>
                                        <li>After defining shifts and policies, you can start onboarding employees by going to Company -> Employee.</li>
                                        <li>
                                            If you don't want to onboard employees one by one, you can onboard bulk employees through Excel. For that, go to Utilities -> Import Employee Excel. Just get the template and start importing bulk employees.
                                        </li>
                                        <li>If you want to onboard employees one by one, click on the '+' button, fill in the necessary details, and save it. Isn't it easy?</li>
                                        <li>This is the whole onboarding process.</li>

                                    </ul>
                                </div>
                            </div>

                        </div>
                    </div>
                </section>
                <section id="Attendance">
                    <h1 class="title">Attendance</h1>
                    <div class="accordion_data">
                        <div class="accordion">
                            <div class="accordion-item">
                                <div class="accordion-header">
                                    <div class="accordion-title">What happens if an employee forgets to clock in/out?</div>
                                    <div class="accordion-icon">
                                        <i class="fa fa-angle-down" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                                <div class="accordion-body">
                                    <p>The system typically allows manual corrections, which are subject to approval by an authorized admin or manager.</p>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                            <div class="accordion-item">
                                <div class="accordion-header">
                                    <div class="accordion-title">What are the types of punches available in minop for attendance?</div>
                                    <div class="accordion-icon">
                                        <i class="fa fa-angle-down" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                                <div class="accordion-body">
                                    <p>Minop supports four types of punches to provide flexibility in recording employee attendance:</p>
                                    <div>
                                        <p><b><u>Web Punch</u></b></p>
                                        <p>Employees log in to the web portal and mark their attendance online.</p>
                                        <p><b>Use Case:</b>Ideal for remote workers or those using desktops/laptops.</p>
                                        <p>
                                            <b>Key Features:</b>
                                            <ul>
                                                <li>Easy access via browser</li>
                                                <li>Real-time time logging</li>
                                                <li>Can include location or IP restrictions for security</li>
                                            </ul>
                                        </p>
                                    </div>
                                    <div>
                                        <p><b><u>Manual Punch</u></b></p>
                                        <p>Attendance is entered manually by HR/admin in cases where the employee was unable to punch in/out.</p>
                                        <p><b>Use Case:</b>Useful for correcting missed punches or addressing technical issues.</p>
                                        <p>
                                            <b>Key Features:</b>
                                            <ul>
                                                <li>Requires admin access</li>
                                                <li>Subject to approval</li>
                                                <li>Ensures data accuracy</li>
                                            </ul>
                                        </p>
                                    </div>
                                    <div>
                                        <p><b><u>Device Punch</u></b></p>
                                        <p> Employees use hardware-based devices like biometric scanners (fingerprint, RFID) for attendance.</p>
                                        <p><b>Use Case:</b>Suitable for on-site staff in offices, factories, or secured areas.</p>
                                        <p>
                                            <b>Key Features:</b>
                                            <ul>
                                                <li>Fast and reliable</li>
                                                <li>Prevents proxy punching </li>
                                                <li>Direct integration with attendance system</li>
                                            </ul>
                                        </p>
                                    </div>
                                    <div>
                                        <p><b><u>Face Punch</u></b></p>
                                        <p>Employees mark their attendance through facial recognition systems.</p>
                                        <p><b>Use Case:</b>Contactless and hygienic option for secure environments.</p>
                                        <p>
                                            <b>Key Features:</b>
                                            <ul>
                                                <li>Touch-free attendance</li>
                                                <li>High accuracy with AI verification</li>
                                                <li>Reduces physical contact and chances of manipulation</li>
                                            </ul>
                                        </p>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                            <div class="accordion-item">
                                <div class="accordion-header">
                                    <div class="accordion-title">As employee from how many places i can place my attendence correction?</div>
                                    <div class="accordion-icon">
                                        <i class="fa fa-angle-down" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                                <div class="accordion-body">
                                    <p>As employee there four place from where you can place correction</p>
                                    <ul>
                                        <li>From Employee Dashboard</li>
                                        <li>From Attendance Correction Page</li>
                                        <li>From Attencance List Page</li>
                                        <li>Mobile App</li>
                                    </ul>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                            <div class="accordion-item">
                                <div class="accordion-header">
                                    <div class="accordion-title">As an admin, from how many places can I place my attendance correction (and my junior's correction)?</div>
                                    <div class="accordion-icon">
                                        <i class="fa fa-angle-down" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                                <div class="accordion-body">
                                    <p>As Admin there four place from where you can place correction</p>
                                    <ul>
                                        <li>From Employee Dashboard</li>
                                        <li>From Attendance Correction Page</li>
                                        <li>From Attencance List Page</li>
                                        <li>Mobile App</li>
                                    </ul>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </section>
                <section id="Leave">
                    <h1 class="title">leave</h1>
                    <div class="accordion_data">
                        <div class="accordion">
                            <div class="accordion-item">
                                <div class="accordion-header">
                                    <div class="accordion-title">Can we create our own organization-based leave types or do we have to use the default ones?</div>
                                    <div class="accordion-icon">
                                        <i class="fa fa-angle-down" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                                <div class="accordion-body">
                                    Yes, you can create your own leave types and assign them to specific users.For that you have to follow given steps:
                                    <ul>
                                        <li>Go to Leave -> LeaveType</li>
                                        <li>Click on <span style="color:#295097; font-size: 20px;"> + </span> button</li>
                                        <li>Fill the necessary details and save it.</li>
                                    </ul>
                                    <div class="slider-container" id="leave_type">
                                        <div class="slide-wrapper">
                                            <div class="slide-block" id="slide-block-9">
                                                <img src="~/assets/images/faq_img/LeaveType.jpg" alt="Leave Type" />
                                                <div class="hover-buttons">
                                                    <div class="hover_block">
                                                        <button class="downloadBtn" onclick="downloadImage(this)"><i class="fa-solid fa-download"></i></button>
                                                        <button class="fullscreenBtn"><i class="fa fa-expand"></i></button>
                                                    </div>
                                                </div>
                                            </div>

                                        </div>
                                        <button class="slider-btn prev">❮</button>
                                        <button class="slider-btn next">❯</button>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                            <div class="accordion-item">
                                <div class="accordion-header">
                                    <div class="accordion-title">As an employee, from how many places can I apply for leave?</div>
                                    <div class="accordion-icon">
                                        <i class="fa fa-angle-down" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                                <div class="accordion-body">
                                    <p>As an employee, there are three places from where you can apply for leave.</p>
                                    <ul>
                                        <li>From Employee Dashboard</li>
                                        <li>From Leave Request Page</li>
                                        <li>Mobile App</li>
                                    </ul>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                            <div class="accordion-item">
                                <div class="accordion-header">
                                    <div class="accordion-title">As an admin, there are multiple places from where you can apply for your own leave or apply leave on behalf of your juniors.</div>
                                    <div class="accordion-icon">
                                        <i class="fa fa-angle-down" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                                <div class="accordion-body">
                                    <p>As an Admin, there are four places from where you can apply leave.</p>
                                    <ul>
                                        <li>From Employee Dashboard</li>
                                        <li>From Leave Request Page</li>
                                        <li>From On Duty Leave Page</li>
                                        <li>Mobile App</li>
                                    </ul>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                            <div class="accordion-item">
                                <div class="accordion-header">
                                    <div class="accordion-title">What is On Duty Leave?</div>
                                    <div class="accordion-icon">
                                        <i class="fa fa-angle-down" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                                <div class="accordion-body">
                                    <p>On Duty Leave is a special type of leave where the employee is working but unable to punch in due to certain reasons—such as being at a different location or at a client site. In such cases, the employee can apply for On Duty Leave, which is by default considered a paid leave.</p>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                            <div class="accordion-item">
                                <div class="accordion-header">
                                    <div class="accordion-title">What is Paid and Unpaid Leave?</div>
                                    <div class="accordion-icon">
                                        <i class="fa fa-angle-down" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                                <div class="accordion-body">
                                    <p>Paid leave refers to the type of leave that is granted by the company with salary. This means the employee will still receive their regular pay during the leave period.
                                    Unpaid leave, on the other hand, is when the employee takes time off that is not covered by the company, meaning no salary is provided for those days.</p>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                            <div class="accordion-item">
                                <div class="accordion-header">
                                    <div class="accordion-title">As an admin, if I want to restrict employees from applying for more than 'N' days of leave, is there any feature or setting for that?</div>
                                    <div class="accordion-icon">
                                        <i class="fa fa-angle-down" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                                <div class="accordion-body">
                                    <p>Yes, in the Leave module, under the Leave Type page, there is a field called "Maximum Leave Apply". As an admin, you can set the maximum number of leave days (N). If an employee tries to apply for more than that number, the system will show a message indicating the maximum leave limit.</p>
                                    <div class="slider-container" id="Maximum_leave">
                                        <div class="slide-wrapper">
                                            <div class="slide-block" id="slide-block-10">
                                                <img src="~/assets/images/faq_img/MaximumLeaveApply.jpg" alt="Maximum Leave Apply" />
                                                <div class="hover-buttons">
                                                    <div class="hover_block">
                                                        <button class="downloadBtn" onclick="downloadImage(this)"><i class="fa-solid fa-download"></i></button>
                                                        <button class="fullscreenBtn"><i class="fa fa-expand"></i></button>
                                                    </div>
                                                </div>
                                            </div>

                                        </div>
                                        <button class="slider-btn prev">❮</button>
                                        <button class="slider-btn next">❯</button>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                            <div class="accordion-item">
                                <div class="accordion-header">
                                    <div class="accordion-title">Is there any encashable leave option in a particular leave type?</div>
                                    <div class="accordion-icon">
                                        <i class="fa fa-angle-down" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                                <div class="accordion-body">
                                    <p>Yes, there is a checkbox named "Is Encashable" under Leave → Leave Type. When the admin selects this checkbox, that leave type becomes encashable; otherwise, it is not.</p>
                                    <div class="slider-container" id="encasable">
                                        <div class="slide-wrapper">
                                            <div class="slide-block" id="slide-block-11">
                                                <img src="~/assets/images/faq_img/EncashableLeave.jpg" alt="Encashable Leave Option" />
                                                <div class="hover-buttons">
                                                    <div class="hover_block">
                                                        <button class="downloadBtn" onclick="downloadImage(this)"><i class="fa-solid fa-download"></i></button>
                                                        <button class="fullscreenBtn"><i class="fa fa-expand"></i></button>
                                                    </div>
                                                </div>
                                            </div>

                                        </div>
                                        <button class="slider-btn prev">❮</button>
                                        <button class="slider-btn next">❯</button>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                            <div class="accordion-item">
                                <div class="accordion-header">
                                    <div class="accordion-title">Is the carry forward concept available for leave?</div>
                                    <div class="accordion-icon">
                                        <i class="fa fa-angle-down" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                                <div class="accordion-body">
                                    <p>Yes, this feature is available, but it entirely depends on the admin. If the admin allows the carry forward facility, it will be enabled. Additionally, customization options are also available.</p>
