                                <div class="accordion-body">
                                    <p>
                                        <ul>
                                            <li>Log in to your Minop Admin account.</li>
                                            <li>Go to Policy, then click on HR Policy, and select Create Policy.</li>
                                            <li>Enter the policy name. Define the first week off, second week off, half-day policy, and overtime according to company rules, then click Next.</li>
                                            <li>If night shifts are applicable, define the Out Punch Limit and the Time Duration Between Two Punches. Set grace time for Late In and Early Out, then click Next.</li>
                                            <li>You must specify the minimum start time for overtime if it is applicable and set the overtime calculation according to your company policy. If you want to apply the sandwich rule, select the checkbox and define it based on your company policy.</li>
                                            <li>If you want attendance to be marked as present with a single punch, you must select "Any Error Case."</li>
                                        </ul>

                                    </p>
                                    <p>If you want to set the half-day and absent rule based on grace time, you need to:</p>
                                    <ul>
                                        <li>Specify the grace time.</li>
                                        <li>Enter the maximum number of times an employee can use the grace time.</li>
                                    </ul>
                                    <p>
                                        For example, if you set "3" in the late count, it means the grace time is allowed twice. After the second instance, any late arrival beyond the grace time will be marked as a half-day. The same rule applies to absences.
                                        If you want to calculate total working hours from the shift start time to the shift end time, you must select both options. This will function as a fixed shift.
                                        For example, if your shift is from 9:00 to 18:00 and you check in at 8:30 and check out at 18:30, the total working hours will be recorded as 9 if both options are selected.
                                    </p>
